      "default": {
        "additional_info": null,
        "result": {
          "type": "string",
          "value": "PASS"
        },
        "shell": "/usr/bin/osascript -l JavaScript -e 'var s = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.alr\"); var list = ObjC.unwrap(s.objectForKey(\"DenyList\")) || []; (list.some(function(item) { return item.PathPrefix == \"/System/Applications/FaceTime.app\"; }) && s.objectIsForcedForKey(\"DenyList\")) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"'"
      },
      "language": "bash"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The macOS built-in FaceTime.app _MUST_ be disabled, unless FaceTime is an approved collaboration tool.\n\nThe FaceTime.app establishes a connection to Apple's iCloud service, even when security controls have been put in place to disable iCloud access.\n\n[IMPORTANT]\n====\nApple has deprecated the use of link:https://github.com/apple/device-management/blob/eb51fb0cb9626cac4717858556912c257a734ce0/mdm/profiles/com.apple.applicationaccess.new.yaml#L67-L70[application restriction controls], using these controls may not work as expected. Third party software may be required to fulfill the compliance requirements.\n====\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
  "id": "mscp.os_facetime_app_disable_familycontrols",
  "odv": null,
